Stanley Myrick wrote:
> My Cloak of Magic Resistance was hit twice by a rotten stupid rot monster
> and is now thoroughly rotted. Is their a way to repair this damage?

	Yes. There's an item that you may have used before to improve
pieces of armor. Used confused, it will not only repair damage to armor,
but prevent it from being further damaged.

 > (as a
> side question, I know it affects the AC of the Cloak, does it affect the MR
> of the Cloak?)

	No. Rot, rust, burning, or corrosion only affects AC, not any
other properties of the armor, and then only up to the natural AC value
of the armor. That is, it won't take away from any plusses on the armor,
and (assuming it's not negatively enchanted), it'll never do worse than
have no effect on your AC.

